Treated units are simply different: a training program enrolls the already-motivated, a new drug goes to the sickest. Comparing raw group means is hopeless. Matching’s move: for every treated unit, find the untreated unit that looks most like it on the observables, and compare each pair6. The plot below draws every match as a thin line –treated points paired with their nearest control on \(x\), unmatched controls fading into the background.
